; on_abort — runs on every abort ([RS274NGC] ON_ABORT_COMMAND).
; Flush air and blow nozzle off, drawbar up, X limit back to the work area
; (tool change area off), X/Y acceleration restored, vacuum pump on/off pulses
; cleared (the pump itself keeps its state), dust hood up/down pulses cleared
; (the hood keeps its position), X oiler request cleared.
; No queue busters (M66, M61 ...): task never resumes on_abort after one, and the
; stale call stack swallows the next MDI command.

o<on_abort> sub
  M65 P7
  M65 P22
  M65 P0
  M65 P8
  M65 P1
  M65 P2
  M65 P4
  M65 P20
  M65 P21
  M101 P#<_accel_x> Q#<_accel_y>   ; not accel_restore: on_abort stops at a queue buster
o<on_abort> endsub
M2
